    "result": "I implemented `shipping_cost` in `solution.py` following `spec.md`, and wrote 9 tests in `tests/test_solution.py`. All 9 pass with `python -m pytest -q tests`.\n\nThe tests cover the base weight tiers, volumetric weight, zone factors, free shipping, the oversize surcharge, rounding and the two-decimal result, float conversion, and `TypeError`/`ValueError` handling. Inputs are checked for type first, then for range, then for zone. I also made non-finite numbers such as NaN or infinity raise `ValueError`; the spec doesn't mention them, and none of the tests cover that case.",
